---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Surrender" description="Information for anyone needing to surrender a cat to Lucky Penny Kitties, including our surrender fee and how to request a spot.">
  <section class="page-intro">
    <h1>Surrendering a Cat</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="max-width:720px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;">
    <p>
      We understand that surrendering a beloved pet is never an easy decision. Every situation is
      unique, and we know this choice often comes with a great deal of emotion. At Lucky Penny
      Kitties, our goal is to ensure that every cat is safe, cared for, and given the opportunity
      to find a loving forever home.
    </p>
    <p>
      As a <strong>foster-based rescue</strong>, we have limited space and can only accept owner
      surrenders when foster homes or openings are available. <strong>Please note that intake is
      not guaranteed</strong>, as we are often at full capacity due to the overwhelming number of
      cats and kittens in need of assistance.
    </p>
    <p>
      If we are unable to accept your cat immediately, we will do our best to place you on our
      waiting list and contact you as soon as space becomes available.
    </p>

    <div class="callout-box">
      <h2>Please Read: We Are Often at Full Capacity</h2>
      <p>
        Lucky Penny Kitties is a <strong>100% volunteer-run, foster-based rescue</strong> — we have
        no shelter or physical facility of our own. Every cat in our care lives in the home of a
        volunteer foster, which means our space is directly limited by how many foster homes we
        have available at any given moment. That number changes constantly, and there are many
        times when we simply have <strong>no openings at all</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        We wish, more than anything, that we could say yes to every cat who needs us.
        <strong>We can't.</strong> There are far more cats in our community than we currently have
        the volunteers, foster homes, and resources to help, and we never want to make promises we
        can't keep. If we are unable to accept your cat right away, please know it is <em>never</em>
        a reflection of how much we care — it's a reflection of our very real limits as a small,
        all-volunteer organization doing our best with what we have.
      </p>
      <p>
        When we're at capacity, we will do everything we can to offer guidance, resources, or a
        spot on our waiting list rather than leave you without options. We are so grateful for your
        patience and understanding as we work as hard as we possibly can to help as many cats as we
        can, one at a time.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please also understand that we are <strong>not an emergency service</strong>. As an
        all-volunteer team, we do not staff a phone line or monitor messages 24/7. We strive to
        respond to every request as quickly as we possibly can, but please be patient with us as we
        balance this work alongside our jobs, families, and the cats already in our care.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Surrender Fee</h2>
    <p>
      A <strong>$25 surrender fee per cat</strong> is required upon intake. This fee helps offset
      the initial costs of care, including food, litter, veterinary services, vaccinations, and
      other essential supplies, allowing us to continue helping as many animals as possible.
    </p>

    <h2>How to Request a Surrender</h2>
    <p>To begin the surrender process, please complete our <strong>Surrender Request Form</strong>.</p>
    <p>
      When submitting your request, please include as much information as possible, such as recent
      photos, age, personality and temperament, medical history, and any special needs or
      behavioral concerns. The more information you provide, the better we can determine the most
      appropriate placement and timeline for your cat.
    </p>

    <h2>What Happens Next?</h2>
    <p><strong>If an opening is available,</strong> a member of our team will contact you to schedule an intake appointment.</p>
    <p>
      <strong>If we are currently at capacity</strong> — which, as a small, all-volunteer rescue,
      happens more often than we'd like — your request will be added to our waiting list, and we
      will reach out as soon as a foster home or space opens up. We want to help every cat who
      needs us, and even when we aren't able to say yes right away, we won't leave you without
      options.
    </p>
    <p>
      At Lucky Penny Kitties, we believe that asking for help is an act of love. We will never
      judge your circumstances. Our mission is to support both animals and the people who care for
      them while working together to find the best possible outcome for every cat.
    </p>
    <p><strong>Thank you for trusting Lucky Penny Kitties with the care and future of your feline companion.</strong> ❤️🐾</p>

    <div class="button-row">
      <a href="https://forms.gle/uAEoreTaTBY6WFyW9" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="cta">Surrender request form</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
